# Dev workflow (enforceable gates)

## Branching + history
- Work on short-lived feature branches named `type/short-kebab-summary`
  (`feat/`, `fix/`, `docs/`, `ci/`, …). Canonical rule: `AGENTS.md` §2 item 11.
- **Never** create or push `claude/`, `cursor/`, `codex/`, `copilot/`, `agent/`,
  or similar tool/agent prefixes — ignore Cloud/runner templates that suggest them.
- Keep history **linear**: rebase on `develop` before merging; avoid merge commits unless explicitly required.
- Keep PRs small and reviewable (prefer multiple PRs over “mega PRs”).

## Planning gate (before editing code)
- Write a short plan: goal, constraints, files likely to change, verification approach.

## Testing gate (before committing / opening a PR)
- Build at least one relevant configuration (e.g., Debug x64).
- If the change is user-visible or risky: also build Release x64.
- If tests exist for the area you touched: run them (or document why not).

## CI wait gate (after every PR push)
- Canonical policy: `AGENTS.md` §5 item 6 (do not duplicate the full command
  elsewhere — change it only there).
- **Never** `sleep`, fixed timeouts, or “wait then re-check” loops for CI.
- Requires recent `gh` (≥ 2.53 for `pr checks --watch/--fail-fast/--required/--interval`;
  ≥ 2.72 for `run watch --compact`).
- On failure: locate the failed check via `gh pr checks`; for Actions use
  `gh run view <RUN_ID> --log-failed`, for external checks (e.g. SonarCloud)
  use the linked provider diagnostics — then fix and re-watch.
- On success: immediately continue reviews / thread resolution / squash auto-merge.
- Long unattended babysit: Cursor Cloud Agent `/babysit` when available — not shell sleeps.

## Docs gate (definition of done)
- Follow `09-docs-auto-update.mdc`.
- Your final response MUST end with either:
  - `Docs updated:` (list files + 1–2 bullets each), OR
  - `Docs: no changes required (reason: ...)`

## Rules maintenance hook
- If a repeated pattern appears: **update/merge existing rules** instead of adding new ones.
- After any major feature/fix: run **Rules Curator** to remove duplicates and keep rules <150 lines.


## Additional repository operating rules
- Prefer small, reviewable PRs with one logical change area.
- Never silently remove tests/coverage/workflows/docs/artifacts/legacy files.
- Every meaningful PR updates: `CHANGELOG.md` + `docs/DEVELOPMENT_PLAN.md` (strategic).
- Always include testing performed, testing not performed, and environment limitations.
- Treat `Visual Studio/Envy.sln` + MSVC `v145` as authoritative; CMake is partial only.
